      "writtenOn": "2012-08-28T00:50:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You might consider returning an error here and having the caller deal with it, by calling board_hard_reset() or whatever. However it looks like the caller here is the battery driver, so it\u0027s not really any better than just calling it here.\n\nIn principle it is nice if drivers fail and return to their callers.\n\nI suggest you add a return code and error checking to board_pmu_init() also\n\nFinally, I wonder if (due to i2c flakeyness) all this setup code is currently partially failing sometimes, perhaps in a non-critical way and so unnoticed. If so your change may through this up. However from what I can tell this cal is only called in the init stage when the AP is off, so should be safe enough. Right?",
      "revId": "fd3301b50078a6c48ba753d93060eb509bf28fbc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
