      "writtenOn": "2012-08-28T15:05:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree about the return codes, but I\u0027m not sure about it in this exact instance.  Like you said, it\u0027s getting called from another driver, etc.  However it\u0027s also getting called when the chipset turns on, so we\u0027d have to duplicate code there since there\u0027s no other reasonable thing to do when your pmic is all screwed up.  Since there\u0027s nothing else reasonable you\u0027d ever want to do, it seems like it should stay bundled in with it to me.\n\nIt\u0027s possible that one or more of these writes fail and go unnoticed, but it should be very unlikely the reason you stated.  Additionally, if the pmu isn\u0027t responding over i2c then, that will be detected before board_pmu_init, when it\u0027s trying to run pmu_init_registers and reset the whole board, so it shouldn\u0027t really happen, I don\u0027t think,",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAPn//7J8\u003d",
